<string_table>

	<string id="pick_class_sniper_title">
		<text>Sniper</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pick_class_sniper_descr">
		<text>Specializes in long-range and lethal damage. Prefers sniper rifles, pistols and, to a lesser extent, assault rifles. For greater convenience, uses medium and light armor. Fast and agile, has high resistance to radiation and damage from anomalies, but tolerates physical and psi damage worse. \n \n
		• Speed +10% \n
		• Weight -10 kg</text>
	</string>

	<string id="pick_class_trooper_title">
		<text>Trooper</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pick_class_trooper_descr">
		<text>A versatile fighter capable of both close and ranged combat. The most effective choice of weapons is an assault rifle, a submachine gun and explosives. Although not as good, he is also able to use a shotgun. Can wear heavy, medium or scientific armor. Has medium resistance to anomalies and physical damage, but low to radiation and psi damage. \n \n
		• No bonuses or penalties</text>
	</string>

	<string id="pick_class_jugger_title">
		<text>Heavy infantry</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pick_class_jugger_descr">
		<text>A melee fighter. Specializes in absorbing physical damage and demoralizing the enemy. Best handled with heavy weapons such as shotguns and machine guns, as well as melee weapons. Just in case, he can also have a submachine gun with him. Wears heavy armor and has a high resistance to psi and physical damage, but is more vulnerable to radiation and anomalies. \n \n
		• Speed -10% \n
		• Weight +10 kg</text>
	</string>

	<string id="pick_class_monster_hunter_title">
		<text>Monster hunter</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pick_class_monster_hunter_descr">
		<text>A specialist in the mutants elimination. He has average skills in using any type of weapon, except explosives. He is able to wear any armor, but has additional small bonuses for medium armor. High protection against rupture, impact and psi damage, average from anomalies. An excellent choice for hunting mutants, but does not stand out much in combat against humans. \n \n
		• Speed +5% \n
		• Weight -5 kg</text>
	</string>

	<string id="pick_class_merc_title">
		<text>Bounty hunter</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pick_class_merc_descr">
		<text>A soldier of fortune who has good skills with almost all types of weapons. Due to the number of shootouts he has to go through, he prefers medium or heavy armor. High ballistic and explosion protection, average against anomalies. A wide range of skills to complete contracts, from lethal damage and explosives, to disguise and surprise kills. A great choice for hunting stalkers, but not particularly good against mutants. \n \n
		• Speed -5% \n
		• Weight +5 kg</text>
	</string>

	<string id="pick_class_assassin_title">
		<text>Assassin</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pick_class_assassin_descr">
		<text>A dexterous master of disguise, stealth and silent kills. Special skills require a subtle approach and appropriate weapons, so he prefers light weapons: submachine guns, pistols and melee weapons. He is able to use medium or scientific armor if he wants to disguise himself as an enemy, or light if he needs to sneak in unnoticed. Focuses on silent, surprise attacks and deadly backstabbing. Not suitable for direct confrontations at any distance. \n \n
		• Speed +10% \n
		• Weight -10 kg \n
		• Able to gain experience of "Defensive" from stealth/disguise</text>
	</string>


